# GBD hashes for Tier D (https://benchmark-database.de/file/<hash>); fetch.py
# --tier D  ->  benchmarks/cache/tierD/<filename>.  Frozen 2026-08-03 from the
# meta sqlite (curl https://benchmark-database.de/getdatabase), selection:
#   SELECT hash FROM track WHERE value IN ('main_2024','main_2025')
# 793 distinct instances = the full SC2024 (400) + SC2025 (400) main tracks with
# 7 content-identical instances shared between the tracks listed once.  The
# blocks below mirror tools/bench/tiers/D.list exactly, and are what a per-track
# (e.g. SC25-only, gate T4) score is reconstructed from.  Where GBD holds
# several filenames for one hash, the lexicographically smallest is used.
# Rationale, composition, and the retained-UNKNOWN decision: see D.list header.
#
